  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Groundwater Model for the Kingdom and 2 Integrated Hydrological Model for the Kingdom</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">An ambitious program for the investigations of its major surface and groundwater resources, for the monitoring of these resources, for the study of hydrological resources (research side), and for the management of the resources (management side).</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Groundwater and Hydrological Model developed for the Kingdom</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A key initiative led by UNDP specialists has been the establishment of the Centre for Water Management and Control. The Centre was able to revive the legacy electronic database that was otherwise inaccessible and outdated. UNDP experts are leading other efforts to enhance the performance of existing remote water monitoring systems for groundwater and surface water. Remote sensing applications to water regulations and monitoring have also been developed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conduct Water data analysis in real-time, classifying and analysing data using various methods, including modelling and remote sensing, and evaluate and document the daily data that come from other systems related to the water sector;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP had previously completed an extensive proposal to design, implement and govern an integrated water management information system (IWMIS). The UNDP proposal covered data acquisition (e.g. automatic water abstraction metering and transmission), storage and processing to facilitate real-time IWRM decision-making. Water sources were to include aquifers, surface water, treated sewage effluent
(TSE) and desalinated sea water. IWMIS was also to include linkages to the other government and private sector organizations involved in integrated water resources management (IWRM) including planning and implementation.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Major Groundwater Studies conducted and models developed</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Demand &amp; Supply Model for (KSA) the Kingdom up to 2050 has been completed and submitted. 
&#x2022;	Major Groundwater Studies have closed, and models have been developed for: Khuff-Jilh-Minjur; Wajid; Wasia-Biyadh-Aruma; Rub&#x2019; Al Khali; Western Coastal Plain National Water Strategy developed and submitted 
&#x2022;	National Water Law has been drafted and submitted. 
&#x2022;	Database System: Restoration of various old databases and rescue of data. 
&#x2022;	Formal Establishment of &#x201c;National Water Research and Studies Center&#x201d; 
&#x2022;	Formal Establishment of &#x201c;Water Management and Control Center&#x201d; including the &#x201c;Hydroinformatics Lab&#x201d;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
